<!--
  The notification icon.

  Android renders this as a silhouette in the status bar: every non-transparent
  pixel becomes white regardless of what colour is declared, so it has to read
  as a shape at 24dp with no colour and no interior detail to lean on. The stock
  `ic_dialog_info` and `stat_notify_error` that were here before are the system's
  own icons — a notification wearing them looks like it came from Android rather
  than from an app, which is the one thing a status-bar icon must not do.

  This is Simba's mark: a filled disc with a bite taken out of the upper right,
  the same gesture as the launcher, legible down to 18px.
-->
